Therefore, the Trial Court had no alternative than to grant a decree in favour of the plaintiff on the following terms:
(i) It is declared that the plaintiff had right to call upon the defendants to execute absolute sale in favour of the plaintiff;
(ii) It is further declared that the proceedings initiated by defendants as on 07.04.2005 are void and enforceable, ultravires of KIDAB Act, and not enforceable;
(ii) it is further declared that the defendants are bound to execute the sale deed in favour of the plaintiff and the defendants are restrained from interfering with the possession of the plaintiff in suit schedule property.
